  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Consider a sample of size ${n}_{1}=62$ from a population with standard deviation ${\\sigma }_{1}=2$ and a sample of size ${n}_{2}=37$ from a population with standard deviation ${\\sigma }_{2}=3.1.$ Given that the samples are independent and the sample means are ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}=5$ and  ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}=2,$ find a $90%$ confidence interval for the difference ${\\mu }_{1}-{\\mu }_{2}$ between the corresponding population means.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z>1.645)=0.05,$ where $Z∼N(0,1).$*",
